-- Both sides of every threshold the text states ("greater than 1,800" means exactly 1,800 is not over), and arithmetic
-- properties checked by evaluation. The thresholds are the text's; the figures on either side of them are this file's.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mg-nouns`
IMPORT `mg-concentration`
IMPORT `mg-frameworks`
IMPORT `mg-rebuttal`
IMPORT `mg-test-fixtures`

§ `Boundaries and properties`

§§ `2.1 Guideline 1: the three thresholds of the table`

-- "Markets with an HHI greater than 1,800 are highly concentrated" ([pdf page 6 of 51]).
#ASSERT NOT (`highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 1800)
#ASSERT `highly concentrated, by an HHI of` 1800.01
-- "a change of more than 100 points is a significant increase": shares of 10 and 5 give exactly 100 (footnote 14's 2ab).
#ASSERT `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 10 5 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT NOT (`a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` (`the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 10 5))
#ASSERT `a significant increase, by a change in HHI of` (`the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 10 5.01)
-- "a share over thirty percent": a 20% and a 10% firm make exactly 30, which is not over.
#ASSERT NOT (`a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` (20 PLUS 10))
#ASSERT `a merged firm's share over thirty percent, by a share of` 30.01
-- Footnote 21: "A concentrated market is one with an HHI greater than 1,000".
#ASSERT NOT (`concentrated, by an HHI of` 1000)
#ASSERT `concentrated, by an HHI of` 1000.01
#ASSERT `the concentration band of an HHI of` 1000 EQUALS `not concentrated (HHI at most 1,000)`
#ASSERT `the concentration band of an HHI of` 1800 EQUALS `concentrated but not highly concentrated (HHI greater than 1,000, at most 1,800)`

-- Each limb needs both of its parts: one at the boundary defeats it.
#ASSERT NOT (`the HHI limb of the presumption is met by` 1800 101)
#ASSERT NOT (`the HHI limb of the presumption is met by` 1801 100)
#ASSERT `the HHI limb of the presumption is met by` 1801 101
#ASSERT NOT (`the share limb of the presumption is met by` 30 101)
#ASSERT NOT (`the share limb of the presumption is met by` 31 100)
#ASSERT `the share limb of the presumption is met by` 31 101
-- Either limb is enough; neither, no presumption.
#ASSERT `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` 1801 101 0 EQUALS `the Agencies presume the merger may substantially lessen competition, unless sufficiently disproved or rebutted`
#ASSERT `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` 1000 101 31 EQUALS `the Agencies presume the merger may substantially lessen competition, unless sufficiently disproved or rebutted`
#ASSERT `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` 5000 100 90 EQUALS `no structural presumption arises under Guideline 1, and the other Guidelines may still apply`

-- A whole market with a significant increase that stays under 1,800: nine firms, built for this test.
-- Parties 10 and 6 (change 120, merged share 16); rivals 20, 20, 20, 10, 6, 4, 4: pre-merger 100+36+400+400+400+100+36+16+16
-- = 1,504, post-merger 1,504 + 120 = 1,624. Not highly concentrated, share not over 30: no presumption.
`a market under 1,800` MEANS LIST (`a party with a share of` "P" 10), (`a party with a share of` "Q" 6), (`a rival with a share of` "R1" 20), (`a rival with a share of` "R2" 20), (`a rival with a share of` "R3" 20), (`a rival with a share of` "R4" 10), (`a rival with a share of` "R5" 6), (`a rival with a share of` "R6" 4), (`a rival with a share of` "R7" 4)
#ASSERT `the pre-merger HHI of` `a market under 1,800` EQUALS 1504
#ASSERT `the post-merger HHI of` `a market under 1,800` EQUALS 1624
#ASSERT `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` (`the post-merger HHI of` `a market under 1,800`) (`the change in HHI of` `a market under 1,800`) (`the merged firm's share in` `a market under 1,800`) EQUALS `no structural presumption arises under Guideline 1, and the other Guidelines may still apply`

§§ `2.1 Guideline 1: arithmetic properties`

-- Footnote 14's 2ab is the recomputed difference of the two HHIs, for two parties, whatever the rest of the market.
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `a market under 1,800` EQUALS `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 10 6
`a 30 and a 1` MEANS LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 30), (`a party with a share of` "B" 1), (`a rival with a share of` "C" 69)
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `a 30 and a 1` EQUALS `the change in HHI from merging firms with shares` 30 1
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `a 30 and a 1` EQUALS 60
-- Three parties: the change is twice the sum of the pairwise products (2(ab + bc + ca)), which is 2ab applied pair by pair.
`three parties` MEANS LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 10), (`a party with a share of` "B" 20), (`a party with a share of` "C" 30), (`a rival with a share of` "D" 40)
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `three parties` EQUALS 2 TIMES ((10 TIMES 20) PLUS (20 TIMES 30) PLUS (30 TIMES 10))
#ASSERT `the merged firm's share in` `three parties` EQUALS 60
-- A party with no share in the market (an acquired firm outside it) changes nothing.
`a party outside the market` MEANS LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 40), (`a party with a share of` "B" 0), (`a rival with a share of` "C" 60)
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `a party outside the market` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the post-merger HHI of` `a party outside the market` EQUALS `the pre-merger HHI of` `a party outside the market`

§§ `2.1 Guideline 1: markets the text cannot read (fork G1-2)`

-- Shares that do not add up to 100: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` (LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 20), (`a party with a share of` "B" 5), (`a rival with a share of` "C" 74)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` (LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 20), (`a party with a share of` "B" 5), (`a rival with a share of` "C" 76)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A negative share, even where the shares add up to 100: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` (LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 110), (`a party with a share of` "B" (0 MINUS 10))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No party to the merger in the market: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` (LIST (`a rival with a share of` "A" 50), (`a rival with a share of` "B" 50)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Footnote 13's own six shares of 16.67 add up to 100.02, so the market as the text writes it is one this encoding will
-- not read; the HHI arithmetic on the same shares is still available (mg-tests.l4).
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` (LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" 16.67), (`a party with a share of` "B" 16.67), (`a rival with a share of` "C" 16.67), (`a rival with a share of` "D" 16.67), (`a rival with a share of` "E" 16.67), (`a rival with a share of` "F" 16.67)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same six firms with shares of exactly 100/6 are read. When two of them merge, the change is 2 x (100/6)^2 = 555.56
-- and the post-merger HHI 1,666.67 + 555.56 = 2,222.22, over 1,800, so the HHI limb raises the presumption (and the
-- merged share, 33.33, is over 30 too).
`two of six equal firms merge` MEANS LIST (`a party with a share of` "A" (100/6)), (`a party with a share of` "B" (100/6)), (`a rival with a share of` "C" (100/6)), (`a rival with a share of` "D" (100/6)), (`a rival with a share of` "E" (100/6)), (`a rival with a share of` "F" (100/6))
#ASSERT `the change in HHI of` `two of six equal firms merge` EQUALS 20000/36
#ASSERT `the post-merger HHI of` `two of six equal firms merge` EQUALS (10000/6) PLUS (20000/36)
#ASSERT `the Guideline 1 presumption on the metrics` (`the post-merger HHI of` `two of six equal firms merge`) (`the change in HHI of` `two of six equal firms merge`) (`the merged firm's share in` `two of six equal firms merge`) EQUALS `the Agencies presume the merger may substantially lessen competition, unless sufficiently disproved or rebutted`
#ASSERT isJust (`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 1 of` `two of six equal firms merge`)

§§ `2.3 Guideline 3: the reading of "highly concentrated" (fork G3-1)`

GIVEN post IS A NUMBER
      change IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Guideline 3 facts`
`structure only` MEANS `Guideline 3 facts` WITH
    `post-merger HHI of the market` IS post
    `change in HHI of the market` IS change
    `firms with a substantial share appear to have coordinated, or attempted to, before` IS FALSE
    `the merger eliminates a maverick or significantly changes its incentives` IS FALSE
    `secondary factors the evidence shows` IS EMPTY
    `response factors the evidence shows` IS EMPTY

-- The discriminating case: a market already highly concentrated (2,000) where the merger adds only 50. 2.3.A's primary
-- factor needs "a merger that significantly increases concentration", so it is absent; section 1's "In a market that is
-- not highly concentrated, the Agencies investigate" does not reach it either. Under reading (a) of fork G3-1 the
-- Agencies would infer harm here; the encoding takes reading (b) and does not.
#ASSERT NOT ((`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 3 of` (`structure only` 2000 50))'s `the Agencies infer, subject to rebuttal, that the merger may substantially lessen competition`)
#ASSERT NOT ((`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 3 of` (`structure only` 2000 50))'s `the Agencies investigate whether facts suggest a greater risk than structure alone`)
-- Each side of 1,800 and of 100.
#ASSERT NOT (`the market is presumptively susceptible to coordination, under 2.3.A` (`structure only` 1800 101))
#ASSERT `the market is presumptively susceptible to coordination, under 2.3.A` (`structure only` 1801 101)
#ASSERT NOT (`the market is presumptively susceptible to coordination, under 2.3.A` (`structure only` 1801 100))
#ASSERT (`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 3 of` (`structure only` 1800 101))'s `the Agencies investigate whether facts suggest a greater risk than structure alone`
#ASSERT NOT ((`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 3 of` (`structure only` 1801 101))'s `the Agencies investigate whether facts suggest a greater risk than structure alone`)

§§ `2.4 Guideline 4: concentrated means an HHI greater than 1,000`

GIVEN m IS A `Concentration of the market entered`
GIVETH A `Guideline 4 facts`
`both elements found in` MEANS `Guideline 4 facts` WITH
    `the market entered` IS m
    `a merging firm had a reasonable probability of entering other than through an anticompetitive merger` IS TRUE
    `that entry offered a substantial likelihood of deconcentration or other significant procompetitive effects` IS TRUE
    `there is substantial direct evidence that the effect of that entry would be de minimis` IS FALSE
    `entry evidence the record shows` IS EMPTY
    `a current participant could reasonably consider a merging firm a potential entrant` IS TRUE
    `that potential entrant has a likely influence on existing competition` IS TRUE
    `influence evidence the record shows` IS EMPTY

#ASSERT NOT (`actual potential competition: the elements of 2.4.A are met` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1000)))
#ASSERT `actual potential competition: the elements of 2.4.A are met` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1000.01))
#ASSERT NOT (`perceived potential competition: the elements of 2.4.B are met` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1000)))
#ASSERT `perceived potential competition: the elements of 2.4.B are met` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1000.01))
-- The suggestion of 2.4.A needs a highly concentrated market: 1,800 is not, 1,800.01 is.
#ASSERT NOT (`the second element of 2.4.A is suggested by high concentration` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1800)))
#ASSERT `the second element of 2.4.A is suggested by high concentration` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 1800.01))
-- A future market has no HHI, so the suggestion never arises there, though the market may be concentrated (footnote 23).
#ASSERT NOT (`the second element of 2.4.A is suggested by high concentration` (`both elements found in` (`a future market not yet commercialized` TRUE)))
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 4 of` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` (0 MINUS 1))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT isJust (`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 4 of` (`both elements found in` (`a market whose HHI is` 10000)))

§§ `2.5 Guideline 5: footnote 30's fifty percent`

#ASSERT `what footnote 30 says of a foreclosure share of` (JUST 50.01) FALSE EQUALS `the Agencies generally infer the merged firm has or approaches monopoly power over the related product`
#ASSERT `what footnote 30 says of a foreclosure share of` (JUST 50) FALSE EQUALS `no inference from the share, and footnote 30 says nothing of a share of exactly fifty percent`
#ASSERT `what footnote 30 says of a foreclosure share of` (JUST 49.99) FALSE EQUALS `no inference from the share, and the merger may still substantially lessen competition`
#ASSERT `what footnote 30 says of a foreclosure share of` (JUST 50) TRUE EQUALS `no inference from the share, and footnote 30 says nothing of a share of exactly fifty percent`

GIVEN share IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Guideline 5 facts`
`a share with significance` MEANS `Guideline 5 facts` WITH
    `the foreclosure share` IS share
    `there is countervailing evidence on monopoly power over the related product` IS FALSE
    `other evidence shows the merged firm has or approaches monopoly power over the related product` IS FALSE
    `the related product is competitively significant` IS TRUE
    `the merged firm's ability to limit access is otherwise shown` IS FALSE
    `the merged firm has the incentive to limit access` IS TRUE
    `considerations the evidence shows` IS EMPTY
    `rivals would continue to access the related product after the merger` IS FALSE
    `the merged firm would gain or increase visibility into rivals' competitively sensitive information` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT (`market structure shows the merged firm's ability to weaken or exclude dependent rivals` (`a share with significance` (JUST 50)))
#ASSERT `market structure shows the merged firm's ability to weaken or exclude dependent rivals` (`a share with significance` (JUST 50.01))
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 5 of` (`a share with significance` (JUST 100.01)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading under Guideline 5 of` (`a share with significance` (JUST (0 MINUS 0.01))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT isJust (`the Agencies' reading under Guideline 5 of` (`a share with significance` (JUST 100)))

§§ `3.1 footnote 62: above liquidation value (liquidation value 100 in every fixture)`

-- An offer of exactly 100 is not "above the liquidation value": footnote 62 does not call it reasonable, and does not
-- call it unreasonable. Rejected, it decides the bar, so the answer is NOTHING (fork FF-2); 100.01 is reasonable and
-- bars the claim.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100 FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100.01 FALSE TRUE TRUE)))) EQUALS JUST (`Failing firm finding` WITH
    `requirement A: a grave probability of business failure` IS TRUE
    `requirement B: prospects of reorganization dim or nonexistent` IS TRUE
    `requirement C: the acquirer is the only available purchaser` IS TRUE
    `a reasonable alternative offer was rejected, so the business cannot be claimed failing` IS TRUE
    `the Agencies accept the failing firm defense` IS FALSE)
-- Open and less dangerous, an offer of exactly 100 decides requirement C: NOTHING. At 100.01 it defeats requirement C.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`requirement C of the failing firm defense is shown` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100.01 TRUE TRUE FALSE))))
-- Open and no less dangerous, an offer of exactly 100 decides nothing either way: the defense is accepted.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE))) EQUALS JUST (`Failing firm finding` WITH
    `requirement A: a grave probability of business failure` IS TRUE
    `requirement B: prospects of reorganization dim or nonexistent` IS TRUE
    `requirement C: the acquirer is the only available purchaser` IS TRUE
    `a reasonable alternative offer was rejected, so the business cannot be claimed failing` IS FALSE
    `the Agencies accept the failing firm defense` IS TRUE)
-- One unclassifiable offer makes the whole answer NOTHING even beside a reasonable one.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 150 FALSE TRUE TRUE), (`an offer of` 90 FALSE TRUE TRUE))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A negative liquidation value or price is impossible.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (0 MINUS 1) EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing firm claim` (`a failing firm claim of` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` (0 MINUS 5) FALSE TRUE FALSE))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A liquidation value of 0: any positive offer is above it.
#ASSERT `the offer is a reasonable alternative offer, by footnote 62` (`an offer of` 0.01 FALSE FALSE FALSE) 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `3.1 footnote 64: a failing division at liquidation value 100`

-- An offer of exactly 100, keeping the assets and less dangerous, would decide condition 2: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`a failing division claim of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`condition 2 of footnote 64 is shown` (`a failing division claim of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100.01 TRUE TRUE FALSE))))
-- The same offer of 100 taking the assets out of the market does not meet condition 2's description, so it decides
-- nothing: the claim may be credited.
#ASSERT (`the Agencies' reading of the failing division claim` (`a failing division claim of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 100 (LIST (`an offer of` 100 TRUE FALSE FALSE)))) EQUALS JUST (`Failing division finding` WITH
    `condition 1: a persistently negative cash flow, not economically justified` IS TRUE
    `condition 2: no reasonable alternative offer keeping the assets in the market and less dangerous` IS TRUE
    `a reasonable alternative offer for the division was rejected` IS FALSE
    `the Agencies may credit the claim that the division's assets would exit` IS TRUE)

§§ `3.2 timeliness: before the effect, strictly`

#ASSERT `the entry is timely` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 23.99 24 TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is timely` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 24 24 TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is timely` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 0 0 TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `the entry is timely` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 0 1 TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`an entry claim of` `entry` (0 MINUS 1) 24 TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the Agencies' reading of the entry claim` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 12 (0 MINUS 1) TRUE TRUE `a full replication of A` FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- No comparison at all: no merging party is replicated, so the entry is not sufficient.
#ASSERT NOT (`the entry is sufficient` (`an entry claim of` `entry` 12 24 TRUE TRUE EMPTY FALSE FALSE))

§§ `3.3 properties`

-- Credited implies cognizable, for no departure and for each single departure.
`every single departure` MEANS LIST (LIST "vague"), (LIST "outside the market"), (LIST "not substantial"), (LIST "an alternative"), (LIST "no contract evidence"), (LIST "not verified"), (LIST "merely benefits the firms"), (LIST "not shown to prevent"), (LIST "worsens terms"), (LIST "separate market"), (LIST "not of the magnitude"), (LIST "tends to monopoly"), (LIST "prevents monopoly")
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD (NOT (`the efficiencies are credited, departing by` d)) OR `the efficiencies are cognizable, departing by` d) (EMPTY FOLLOWED BY `every single departure`)
-- Of the thirteen single departures, exactly two leave the efficiencies credited: "prevents monopoly" alone (no tendency
-- to monopoly, so the clause does not bite) and none other; and "tends to monopoly" alone defeats crediting. So exactly
-- one is credited.
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `the efficiencies are credited, departing by` d) `every single departure`) EQUALS 1
-- Eight of the departures defeat cognizability (the four criteria); five leave it cognizable.
#ASSERT count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD `the efficiencies are cognizable, departing by` d) `every single departure`) EQUALS 5
